  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1140 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nHigh pressure continues to shift more over the Desert Southwest\nthrough the weekend which will allow temperatures to fall to\nslightly above normal with high 90s being common. Storm chances\nwill also peak around late Thursday into Friday as northwest flow\nbecomes more prominent and stronger. This will allow shortwave\nenergy to traverse the area providing more widespread lift. The\nbig questions now is with quality of moisture and instability,\nalong with position of a weak cold front going into Friday. If the\nstorm activity ends up being more widespread late Thursday,\ntemperatures may be a bit cooler than currently forecasted leading\nto more 90s on Friday rather than near 100. \n\nWard",
